pthreads: __sync_val_compare_and_swap returns the old value, as GCC's builtin

On m68k pthread.c defines __sync_val_compare_and_swap itself, under Disable().
It returned the new value when the swap was made and the expected value when
it was not, so a caller could not tell what was there. Its three callers in
this file (pthread_spin_lock and pthread_spin_trylock) were written for that.

It now returns the value that was there, like GCC's builtin and every other
compiler's, and the spinlocks test for != 0 (the lock was held). The MorphOS
branch of pthread_spin_lock, which uses the real builtin, was inverted the
same way and is right now too.

